[?1049h[1;24r[1;1H[J[7m  UW PICO 5.09                           New Buffer                             [27m[23;1H[K[24;1H[K[23;1H[7m^[27m[7mG[27m Get Help  [7m^[27m[7mO[27m WriteOut  [7m^[27m[7mR[27m Read File [7m^[27m[7mY[27m Prev Pg   [7m^[27m[7mK[27m Cut Text  [7m^[27m[7mC[27m Cur Pos   [K[24;1H[7m^[27m[7mX[27m Exit      [7m^[27m[7mJ[27m Justify   [7m^[27m[7mW[27m Where is  [7m^[27m[7mV[27m Next Pg   [7m^[27m[7mU[27m UnCut Text[7m^[27m[7mT[27m To Spell  [K[3;1H[22;1H                                                                                [22;33H[7m[ Reading file ][27m[22;1H                                                                                [22;32H[7m[ Read 404 lines ][27m[1;1H[J[7m  UW PICO 5.09                        File: README.md                           [27m[3;1H# fux-vt-compare: fux-vt beside other terminal emulators[5;1HAn excluded package with its own lockfile. It runs fux-vt beside a panel of[6;1Hother terminal emulators ("engines"):[8;1H- engines linked into the binary: Ghostty's core (libghostty-vt), alacritty_ter$[9;3Hlibvterm, avt, wezterm-term and the vt100 crate;[10;1H- engines run as processes of their own: xterm.js (`@xterm/headless` under[11;3HNode), tmux, and xterm itself under Xvfb.[13;1HEvery engine gets the same output. After each piece of it, and each resize,[14;1Heach engine's screen is compared with fux-vt's, cell by cell, along with the[15;1Hcursor, the modes, soft wraps, the title, cursor reports and recent history.[16;1Hfux-vt fails a case only where the engines outvote it (see "The vote"). A[17;1Hfailing case is shrunk to the smallest one that still fails and printed with[18;1Hthe command that replays it. `bench` times every engine on the same[19;1Hworkloads. The corpus (`corpus/`) holds what real programs wrote to a[20;1Hterminal, recorded by `record`.[23;1H[K[24;1H[K[23;1H[7m^[27m[7mG[27m Get Help  [7m^[27m[7mO[27m WriteOut  [7m^[27m[7mR[27m Read File [7m^[27m[7mY[27m Prev Pg   [7m^[27m[7mK[27m Cut Text  [7m^[27m[7mC[27m Cur Pos   [K[24;1H[7m^[27m[7mX[27m Exit      [7m^[27m[7mJ[27m Justify   [7m^[27m[7mW[27m Where is  [7m^[27m[7mV[27m Next Pg   [7m^[27m[7mU[27m UnCut Text[7m^[27m[7mT[27m To Spell  [K[3;1Hterminal, recorded by `record`.[K[5;1HIt is not built or run by fux's own gates. It needs Zig, a Ghostty[K[6;1Hcheckout, libvterm's source and, for the engines in their own processes,[7;1HNode, tmux, xterm and Xvfb. `run.sh` fetches the first three.[8;1H[K[9;1HNo engine is the truth. When the panel outvotes fux-vt, the difference says[10;1Hwhere to look. xterm's behaviour and the standards decide which side is   [11;1Hright. Some differences are choices fux-vt makes on purpose, and each family[12;1Hbelow records which.[13;1H[K[14;1H## Running it[K[15;1H[K[16;1H```sh[K[17;2Hux-vt/compare/run.sh                       # families expected to agree, 20000$[18;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh engines               # which engines run here, which vot$[19;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh cases                 # the named cases beside every engi$[20;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh verdicts              # the families with a recorded verd$[21;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh matrix                # family by engine: % of cases each$[3;1H[22;1H                                                                                [22;1H[7mSearch:                                                                         [22;9H[27m[23;15H[7mY[27m FirstLine [7m^[27m[7mR[27m Replace   [7m^[27m[7mT[27m LineNumber[7m^[27m[7mO[27m End of Par             [K[24;2H[7mC[27m Cancel    [7m^[27m[7mV[27m LastLine  [7m^[27m[7m^[27m Optns Menu[7m^[27m[7mW[27m Start of P[7m^[27m[7mU[27m FullJustif             [K[7m[22;9H                                                                        [22;9Hr                                                                       [22;10He                                                                      [22;11Hf                                                                     [22;12Hl                                                                    [22;13Ho                                                                   [22;14Hw                                                                  [22;15H[27m[22;1H                                                                                [3;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh verdicts              # the families with a recorded verd$[4;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh matrix                # family by engine: % of cases each$[5;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh bench                 # MB/s for every engine on every wo$[6;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh bench --engines ghostty corpus   # each recording alone t$[7;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh --list                # the families, their status and re$[8;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh survey                # each family alone: how often it f$[9;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh run --family sgr --family text --cases 2000 --seed 7 [10;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh run --engines ghostty,libvterm,xterm   # any panel[11;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh replay --engines all --size 1x5 'abcde\x08X'[K[12;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh --no-reflow           # fux-vt set up as fux sets it up[13;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh corpus                # the recordings beside xterm and t$[14;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh corpus --show vim     # one recording, and fux-vt's scree$[15;1Hfux-vt/compare/run.sh inventory > fux-vt/compare/corpus/INVENTORY.md   # what t$[16;1Hfux-vt/compare/corpus/record.sh [NAME...]   # record the corpus again (see "The$[17;23H--cargo test          # any cargo subcommand, in the same[18;23H--cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings[K[19;1H```[K[20;1H[K[21;1HThe first run fetches Zig 0.16.0, Ghostty and libvterm into[K[23;1H[K[24;1H[K[23;1H[7m^[27m[7mG[27m Get Help  [7m^[27m[7mO[27m WriteOut  [7m^[27m[7mR[27m Read File [7m^[27m[7mY[27m Prev Pg   [7m^[27m[7mK[27m Cut Text  [7m^[27m[7mC[27m Cur Pos   [K[24;1H[7m^[27m[7mX[27m Exit      [7m^[27m[7mJ[27m Justify   [7m^[27m[7mW[27m Where is  [7m^[27m[7mV[27m Next Pg   [7m^[27m[7mU[27m UnCut Text[7m^[27m[7mT[27m To Spell  [K[12;28H[1;35H[7mFile: README.md                     Modified[27m[12;23Hcorpus                # the recordings beside xterm and t$[13;30H--show vim     # one recording, and fux-vt's scree[14;23Hinventory > fux-vt/compare/corpus/INVENTORY.md   # what t[15;16Hcorpus/record.sh [NAME...]   # record the corpus again (see "The[16;16Hrun.sh --cargo test          # any cargo subcommand, in the sam[17;31Hclippy --all-targets -- -D warnings[K[18;1H```[K[19;1H   [20;1HThe first run fetches Zig 0.16.0, Ghostty and libvterm into[21;1H`~/.cache/fux-vt-compare` (or `$FUX_VT_COMPARE_CACHE`). It also installs[12;1H[23;1H             [7mY[27m Yes                                                            [K[24;2H[7mC[27m Cancel    [7mN[27m No                                                             [K[22;1H                                                                                [22;1H[7mSave modified buffer (ANSWERING "No" WILL DESTROY CHANGES) ?                    [22;62H[27m[7mNo[27m[23;1H[K[24;1H[K[?1049l